MPL-2.0 (LICENSE-MPL-2.0)

  - the reference implementation: crates/vitrin-core (the trusted core —
    compositor, capability kernel, grant store, realms, consent, dead-man
    switch, flight recorder), crates/vitrin-ipc (the transport),
    crates/vitrin-realm-init (the per-realm namespace helper the core execs,
    and the frame vocabulary the two sides share), and the
    per-app Wayland shim under shim/ — its C sources, its hand-written
    headers, and its own test fixtures.

  Weak copyleft on the TCB is the point: Vitrin's claim is a small,
  auditable trusted core, and a modified capability kernel should not be
  shippable as a black box. MPL's copyleft is per-file, so an application
  running inside a shim is never derivative, and the Larger Work allowance
  (MPL 2.0 §3.3) keeps linking against MIT-licensed wlroots and Smithay
  clean.

  MPL Exhibit B ("Incompatible With Secondary Licenses") is deliberately
  NOT used anywhere in this repository, and must not be added. The advisory
  WLCS module below compiles MPL-2.0 shim sources into a GPL-3.0-only
  combined work; that is lawful only because MPL 2.0 keeps GPL-3.0 as a
  Secondary License (§1.12, §3.3). Exhibit B would switch that off and make
  the module undistributable.

